cmu-mohawk-gunnery-only = Fire the M90 from the dedicated gunnery console.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-seat = You must be buckled into the gunnery seat to fire the M90.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-manual = Take turret control
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-automatic = Restore automatic control
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-control-help = Groundside only. Automatic IFF targeting is the default. Take control while seated, then click the left camera view to aim and fire, or use combat mode in the main view. The preview shows the forward arc and range. Press Mark hostile, then click a visible hostile to track it without firing. CONFIRM automatic fire authorizes engagement until the lock is lost or cleared. Clicking the left camera to fire manually clears tracking. Closing the console restores default automatic control.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ground-only = The chin turret can only be controlled manually while landed.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-busy = Another operator is controlling the chin turret.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-range = The target is outside the chin turret's range.
